Z||000006||LoW_KeY||11-23-2001||05:20 AM||||well I had my old 84 coupe and my friend thought he could handle with it in his friends station wagon they tried for 30 around a corner that was made for 10.  Well they rode on 2 wheels in that car with a bunch of people screaming and running on the corner.<P>Owned a late 90's mustang around the corner guy went squeeling all the way around I just put it in 2nd and slammed on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> he didn't really try much after that.  I think he figured I had a 4 cyl. since I was goin 30 in 4th gear quiet as can be then down shifted to 2nd hehe..<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dragon||11-23-2001||06:52 PM||||I sure that many of us have outdriven other cars.  It is the sport of driving a properly set up Fiero.  Tut the best test I know of is the "Dragon" HWY 129 on the NC / TN there are not a lot of other cars I would like to have up on that road!!  300 plus turns in 11 miles - it is a little two lane road that the bikers go to play   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dragon<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://SpaceCoastFieros.com/dragon.jpg">            <BR>   Space Coast Fieros -&gt; Florida Fiero Council<BR>             Home of the Florida Fiero Weekend <A HREF="http://FloridaFieros.org/daytona2002" TARGET=_blank>http://FloridaFieros.org/daytona2002</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Dragon (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||11-24-2001||03:35 AM||||Just came back from a 'sorting' run to our 'proving grounds' or so we call them.  Curvy little ~1mile section of extreme twisties that also climbs about 800feet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The car is handling great, I think we've really hit it with these new alignment settings...  one hard right-handed up-hill curve, the car will LIFT THE INSIDE WHEEL, then a fraction of a second later, as the car crests the same hill, I actually get some very brief wheelspin... in 2nd gear... (this is a stock 2.8 motor, and fairly grippy tyres, it won't spin at all in first when the clutch is dumped at 3,500rpm... just *GOES*...)<P>We need a Gtech, or a better accelerometer.  But I'm convinced we're now well over 1G.<P>And the car is totally neutural, drift, over or understeer selectable quite easily with the throttle, at any point.  Watch the rear-end though, when it goes, you have to CATCH it ;0)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>Now I've just gotta make it pull as hard in 4th as it does in first....<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||artherd||11-24-2001||03:40 AM||||Forgot to mention, my friend has a '67 mustang that we've been working on as well (351W bored to a 357/5.9litre. 11:1 compression, and we're going to inject it soon, 750cfm carb now. good for ~375bhp.)<P>The car is nothing like what the 1960s saw, it's been converted to a full tubular front suspension, with a new crossmember supporting our rack and pinion steering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  He does have crappy tires though, which are hurting him bad.<P>Anyway, my car was nearly *twice* as fast through these twisties, with almost a 3x horsepower disadvantage.<P>Viva mid-engine!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
